BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ctm-resynthesising-traditional-at-the-extreme-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: CTM Festival: Resynthesising the Traditional 2027 Artisti
 c Lab (At the Extreme)
DESCRIPTION:Resynthesising the Traditional is CTM Festival's long-term init
 iative co-curated by Stas Sharifulla\, taking resynthesis (the computer-mu
 sic method of analysing a sound to extract its components) as a metaphor f
 or critically engaging with tradition and heritage\, against conservative 
 views of culture as frozen and untouchable. The artistic lab at its heart 
 is an open toolbox for artists connecting to the traditional outside exoti
 cisation\, cultural essentialism and uneven power dynamics. THEME\, AT THE
  EXTREME: this edition invites artists and practice-based researchers whos
 e work examines the ethical\, aesthetic and political implications of trad
 itions entangled with extremity: intensity\, transgression\, transformatio
 n\, marginality\, outsiderness\, endurance\, conflict and excess. The call
  explicitly looks past the usual noise\, violence and loud-popular-music t
 ropes and past masculine codings of the extreme\, toward current queer and
  feminist reframings\, treating extremity as a relational condition\, chos
 en or imposed\, produced between majoritarian centres and their minoritari
 an outsides. Guiding questions include what it means to follow a tradition
  to its extreme consequences\, who is allowed to push tradition to its lim
 its and whose practices get framed as inauthentic or dangerous\, what it m
 eans to practise tradition under war\, displacement\, repression or ecolog
 ical crisis\, and how traditions might offer ways of inhabiting extreme ti
 mes. Preference goes to work engaging technological\, bodily\, aesthetic a
 nd theoretical forms at that intersection\, especially in unexpected or ra
 rely recognised ways. WHAT HAPPENS: theory and practice workshops from the
  co-hosts with individual and group exercises\, closed 15 to 20 minute ora
 l presentations by each participant\, a solo public performance or present
 ation (15 to 20 minutes) at a free-entry event\, inputs from specialists s
 uch as artists\, researchers and technologists\, guided individual and gro
 up sonic improvisations\, field trips and site visits\, and feedback sessi
 ons with the co-hosts and curators. AFTERWARDS: participants may propose n
 ew artistic work or research\, solo or in collaborations formed at the lab
 \, to the artistic team\; selected works are shortlisted\, and up to two a
 re commissioned and presented at CTM in January/February 2028. ELIGIBILITY
 : an existing practice tied to (re)connecting with traditional ideas and s
 ounds through a contemporary lens and how that overlaps with the extreme\,
  plus clear ideas or questions about the next step you want to take. Appro
 aches may be technological\, instrument-focused\, compositional\, aestheti
 c\, research-oriented or otherwise. Working knowledge of English is recomm
 ended\, and any concerns about that can be flagged in the form. Up to six 
 participants are selected by co-hosts Karina Utomo (extreme metal vocalist
 \, composer and collaborative artist) and Luigi Monteanni (sound researche
 r and ethnomusicologist completing a PhD at SOAS on extreme metal in Bandu
 ng). The lab is a time-intensive full-day commitment and participants must
  agree to give the short public performance. APPLY through the form with a
  portfolio link (PDF\, max 10 pages\, public access\, works from the last 
 five years\, text kept minimal) and a link to a specific audio track or se
 ction (max five minutes) that best represents your current practice. CTM a
 sks that AI support rather than replace your own voice in the application.
  TIMELINE: deadline 28 September 2026\; participants announced mid to late
  October 2026. Questions to resynth@ctm-festival.de.\n\nOrganisation: CTM 
 Festival\, co-curated by Stas Sharifulla\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Open
  to artists worldwide\; solo artists and projects only.\nAward: Travel bud
 get of up to EUR 300 per person\, plus accommodation and catering for the 
 duration of the lab and a festival pass to CTM 2027 events. Visa fees are 
 supported where required\, and letters of invitation are provided for visa
  or funding applications. NO artist fee or stipend for the lab itself. Aft
 erwards\, up to two new works arising from the lab may be commissioned and
  presented at CTM Festival in January/February 2028. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Seven days: arrival 24 January\, lab 26 to 31 January 2027 (10:0
 0 to 19:00 daily)\, public presentations 26 January\, departure 1 February
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/resyn
 thesising-the-traditional-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/resynthesising-the
 -traditional-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Open to artists worldwide\; solo artists and pro
 jects only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:das-minsk-culinary-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260906
SUMMARY:Deadline: DAS MINSK Culinary Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:DAS MINSK opened in 1977 as a terrace restaurant and now runs a
 s a museum of modern and contemporary art\, and its Culinary Residency bui
 lds on that history by treating cooking as a cultural and artistic practic
 e. From April to July 2027 the selected resident develops an original proj
 ect at the intersection of art\, food and society and presents it as part 
 of the museum's public programme\, opening up new perspectives on art\, fo
 od and social questions and actively engaging visitors. The residency give
 s space to develop new formats and culinary projects across art\, cooking\
 , food\, culture\, sustainability and social issues\, with the museum unde
 rstood as a place of exchange and encounter. ELIGIBILITY: chefs\, artists\
 , food designers and interdisciplinary practitioners whose work engages qu
 estions of community\, memory\, hospitality\, ecology and the future of ea
 ting\; applicants from diverse backgrounds and perspectives are explicitly
  encouraged. SUPPORT: EUR 1\,000 per month\, furnished apartment\, travel 
 reimbursement to the start of the residency\, a Deutschlandticket\, possib
 le coverage of production costs\, museum access and team support. APPLICAT
 ION: a single PDF (max 10 pages\, 5 MB) with a short biography\, portfolio
  or work samples\, a project description (max 2 pages) and a cost estimate
  (max 1 page)\, emailed to residency@dasminsk.de. DEADLINE: 5 September 20
 26\, 11:59pm. Results expected November or December 2026. No fee.\n\nOrgan
 isation: DAS MINSK Kunsthaus in Potsdam\nLocation: Potsdam\, Germany (Max-
 Planck-Strasse 17\, 14473 Potsdam). In-person residency at the museum\; op
 en internationally.\nAward: Stipend of EUR 1\,000 per month for four month
 s (EUR 4\,000 total)\, plus a furnished apartment (accommodation for up to
  three people\, so family can join\, though their travel and living costs 
 are not covered)\, reimbursement of travel expenses to the start of the re
 sidency\, a Deutschlandticket for the duration\, and the possibility of pr
 oduction costs for the proposed project being covered. Access to the museu
 m's exhibitions and relevant work areas\, and support from the museum team
 . One residency awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Four months\, Apri
 l to July 2027\n\nMore: https://dasminsk.de/en/residency?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dasminsk.de/en/residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Potsdam\, Germany (Max-Planck-Strasse 17\, 14473 Potsdam). In-pers
 on residency at the museum\; open internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-biologica-artxscience-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ars Biologica ArtXScience Residency 2027-2028 (Ars Electr
 onica x Ceske Budejovice ECoC 2028)
DESCRIPTION:A fully funded art-science residency from Ars Electronica and C
 eske Budejovice\, European Capital of Culture 2028\, exploring how art and
  science can collaborate on urgent environmental challenges: climate emerg
 ence\, sustainable agriculture\, geoengineering\, permaculture\, water res
 ource management\, and the broader ecological impacts on local communities
 . Selected residents work in direct collaboration with local scientists in
  Ceske Budejovice. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, designers\, creatives and arti
 st collectives with more than 5 years of professional creative practice an
 d documented interdisciplinary work\; experience in community engagement a
 nd science collaborations is essential\; applicants must be 18+\, of any n
 ationality\, and legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. WHAT YOU G
 ET: a EUR 24\,000 package (EUR 6\,000 artist fee\, up to EUR 15\,000 produ
 ction\, up to EUR 3\,000 travel and subsistence) plus one month of housing
  covered separately\; two winners are selected. STRUCTURE: the residency r
 uns January 2027 to April 2028\, with a required on-site stay of up to one
  month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/September 2027\
 , and a March 2028 stay for festival installation\, exhibition and deinsta
 llation. HOW TO APPLY: online form with project title\, a written proposal
  of max 250 words\, a scientific direction statement (max 100 words)\, art
 istic vision (max 100 words)\, community connection plan (max 100 words)\,
  a super short pitch (3 to 30 words)\, 3 to 7 images\, an optional 1-minut
 e video\, a portfolio link and contact information. Two-round selection (o
 nline application then interview)\; winners notified by November 2026. Dea
 dline 28 September 2026 at midnight CET.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electronica 
 and Ceske Budejovice - European Capital of Culture 2028\nLocation: Ceske B
 udejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any nationality aged 18+
  who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Required on-site s
 tays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/
 September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibition and deinstal
 lation.\nAward: EUR 24\,000 total package per winner: EUR 6\,000 artist fe
 e\, up to EUR 15\,000 production budget\, and up to EUR 3\,000 for travel\
 , accommodation and subsistence\, plus a separate budget covering one mont
 h of housing in Ceske Budejovice. Two positions available. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: January 2027 to April 2028\, with on-site blocks in early 2027 
 and March 2028\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars
 -biologica-art-science-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars-biologica-art-scienc
 e-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ceske Budejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any natio
 nality aged 18+ who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Req
 uired on-site stays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional 
 stay in August/September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibiti
 on and deinstallation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:studio-alta-residence-2027-open-calls@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Studio ALTA Residence 2027: four residency open calls (Pr
 ague)
DESCRIPTION:Prague performance venue Studio ALTA announces four residency o
 pen calls for 2027\, all with a single deadline of 10 September 2026. RESE
 ARCH HOUSE (19 to 28 April 2027): a shared residential laboratory for thre
 e art projects or individual artists in the early stages of exploration an
 d experimentation\, or reopening an existing finished work (performance\, 
 installation\, object\, video) to transform it into another form such as a
  workshop\, text or performance-lecture. Includes a 10-day residency\, a f
 ee of CZK 12\,000 per project\, shared studio\, individual workspace and f
 acilitated exchange meetings\; the research output must be shared publicly
  as a work-in-progress in a form based on participants' needs. REST HOUSE 
 (March to November 2027): a five-day residential spa for overloaded collea
 gues from the arts sector\, with no required output or activities\; restri
 cted to people working in production\, dramaturgy\, curation\, PR\, techni
 cal and other supporting artistic professions in the Czech independent sec
 tor. Two guests are chosen by lottery (fee CZK 6\,000 per person)\; the pu
 blic draw is announced 16 September 2026. HOUSE IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD (9 to 
 18 August 2027): for one performative art project created with the local c
 ommunity and designed or adapted for public space in Liben and its surroun
 dings\; this year's call focuses on the 55+ target group. Includes a fee o
 f CZK 30\,000 per project\, rehearsal and indoor facilities (primarily out
 door spaces)\, dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, 
 connections to partner organisations\, and 7 days of intensive production 
 and technical support in the final phase. A public premiere or work-in-pro
 gress in public space at the end of the residency is required. HOUSE OF SW
 EAT (1 to 10 February 2027): for one performative art project designed or 
 adapted for the specific environment of the Studio ALTA sauna and its imme
 diate surroundings\, seeking new ways of working with intimate space\, pro
 ximity to the audience and non-traditional formats. Includes a fee of CZK 
 15\,000 per project\, a 10-day residency\, sauna and rehearsal spaces\, dr
 amaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, and 2 days of int
 ensive final-phase support\; a public work-in-progress or premiere in the 
 sauna within the 9 to 12 February 2027 programme block is required. Projec
 ts at any stage of development can apply to the production calls\, and sel
 ected projects may be included in Studio ALTA's year-round programme. TIME
 LINE: deadline 10 September 2026\; results 3 weeks after the deadline (30 
 September 2026)\; a Q&A Zoom call takes place 10 August 2026 at 3:00 PM. A
 pply via the registration forms on the call page.\n\nOrganisation: Studio 
 ALTA\nLocation: Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Th
 ree of the four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is re
 served for supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independ
 ent sector.\nAward: Residency fees paid to participants: Research House CZ
 K 12\,000 per project\; Rest House CZK 6\,000 per person\; House in the Ne
 ighborhood CZK 30\,000 per project\; House of Sweat CZK 15\,000 per projec
 t. All include workspace at Studio ALTA\; the two production residencies a
 dd dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR support. Free to apply.\nDu
 ration: Programme dependent: 5 to 10 days\, at various points between Febr
 uary and November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Three of t
 he four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is reserved f
 or supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independent sect
 or.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cannes-residence-cinema-de-demain-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: La Résidence du Festival de Cannes (Cinéma de Demain): 
 Screenwriting Residency in Paris
DESCRIPTION:La Résidence of the Festival de Cannes (part of Cinéma de Dem
 ain\, formerly La Cinéfondation) invites 12 directors each year to write 
 their screenplay in Paris. The programme provides a place of residence in 
 the heart of Paris\, a personalised programme accompanying the writing of 
 their scripts\, and a collective programme of forums with film industry pr
 ofessionals. The 12 directors from the two annual sessions present their p
 rojects at the CNC pavilion in Cannes\, giving 10-minute presentations to 
 an audience of professionals and a jury of three film industry personaliti
 es\; the CNC then awards a EUR 5\,000 grant to one director from each sess
 ion\, based on the project that most inspires the jury. The Cinef & Résid
 ence offices serve as a hub where directors meet and schedule private meet
 ings with potential producers. ELIGIBILITY: open to young filmmakers who h
 ave made one or several short films and no more than one feature film\; ca
 ndidates must NOT be residents or citizens of France. Selected filmmakers 
 must stay at the Résidence in Paris for the full session. SESSIONS: two p
 er year\, each lasting four and a half months\, the first running 15 March
  to 31 July and the second 1 October to 15 February. Artistic fields: film
 \, writing\, interdisciplinary. Deadline: 30 September 2026 at 16:00 UTC. 
 Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Festival de Cannes (Cinéma de Demain / La
  Résidence)\nLocation: Paris\, France. Candidates must not be residents o
 r citizens of France.\nAward: Fully supported: a place of residence in cen
 tral Paris\, a personalised script-writing programme\, and a collective pr
 ogramme of forums with film industry professionals. Directors present at t
 he CNC pavilion in Cannes\, where the CNC awards a EUR 5\,000 grant to one
  director per session. Free to apply.\nDuration: Four and a half months pe
 r session (two sessions a year)\n\nMore: https://cinemadedemain.festival-c
 annes.com/en/take-part/register-to-the-residence/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cinemadedemain.festival-cannes.com/en/take-part/register-to-the
 -residence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Candidates must not be residents or citizens of Fr
 ance.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fucina-futura-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fucina Futura 2027 Residency (Marostica\, Italy)
DESCRIPTION:Fucina Futura is an artist residency in Marostica\, a small tow
 n about an hour from Venice\, offering a peaceful setting to develop resea
 rch in close contact with nature and the local community. The project span
 s two locations: the home designed by internationally renowned illustrator
  Elena Xausa near the historic centre\, and the atelier Fucina Ai Gorghi b
 y beloved local painter Daniele Marcon\, ideal for large-scale installatio
 ns. Led by visual artist Lavinia and curator Sofia (Futura Association)\, 
 the program invites residents to develop projects that engage with the com
 munity and the working location\, and encourages artists of any discipline
  to make full use of the large atelier. The central goal is the 'restituti
 on' to citizens\, fostering cultural exchange and community inclusion: thi
 s final phase is tailored to each artist and can take the form of an exhib
 ition\, performance\, workshop\, screening\, talk or informal sharing sess
 ion\, prioritising direct dialogue with the public and the contemporary re
 newal of local tradition. THREE residents are hosted together from 12 Apri
 l to 12 May 2027 and share a spacious house\; they receive a daily fee to 
 cover living expenses\, and travel expenses are also covered. Made possibl
 e by Culture Moves Europe. ELIGIBILITY: only artists residing in one of th
 e Creative Europe countries EXCEPT ITALY may apply. Creative Europe covers
  the 27 EU member states (other than Italy)\, plus Albania\, Armenia\, Bos
 nia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\, Kosovo\, Liechtenstein\, Moldova
 \, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, Tunisia and Ukraine\, 
 and includes the EU's Overseas Countries and Territories and Outermost Reg
 ions (Greenland\; French Guiana\, French Polynesia\, French Southern and A
 ntarctic Territories\, Guadeloupe\, Martinique\, Mayotte\, New Caledonia\,
  Reunion\, Saint Barthelemy\, Saint-Martin\, St. Pierre and Miquelon\, Wal
 lis and Futuna\; Azores\, Madeira\; Canary Islands\; Aruba\, Bonaire\, Cur
 acao\, Saba\, Sint Maarten\, Sint Eustatius). TIMELINE: apply via the Goog
 le Form by 20 August 2026\; selected artists informed by 30 August and mus
 t confirm participation by 8 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Futura Assoc
 iation (Fucina Futura)\, supported by Culture Moves Europe\nLocation: Maro
 stica\, Italy (one hour from Venice). Open to artists resident in a Creati
 ve Europe country except Italy.\nAward: Fully funded: daily fee to cover l
 iving expenses\, travel costs covered\, and shared house accommodation pro
 vided (supported by Culture Moves Europe). No application fee.\nDuration: 
 One month\, 12 April to 12 May 2027\; three residents hosted together\n\nM
 ore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwEmQ2EFrMoukgNorlOLE5kGvGr
 iMX0IdMBObmhfgRlSW-jQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwEmQ2EFrMoukgNorlOLE5kGvGriM
 X0IdMBObmhfgRlSW-jQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Marostica\, Italy (one hour from Venice). Open to artists resident
  in a Creative Europe country except Italy.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-delfina-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Delfina Foundation Residency 2027 (London
 )
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at London's Delfina Fou
 ndation\, one of the UK's best known artist-in-residence programmes\, hous
 ed at 29-31 Catherine Place near Buckingham Palace with space for 6 to 8 i
 nternational residents (own room\, shared kitchen and facilities). Delfina
  promotes artistic exchange and experiment\, offering visual artists and c
 urators a platform to carry out research\, develop ideas and position thei
 r practice within the global discourse\, with introductions to the London 
 art scene and Delfina's international network. The programme includes visi
 ts to museums\, galleries and non-profit platforms\, discussions with Lond
 on-based artists\, portfolio reviews with curators and regular networking 
 lunches\; residents are expected to take part. Applicants are not asked fo
 r a concrete project proposal but must submit a clear motivation: why they
  wish to take part\, what research they want to conduct\, and how it can c
 ontribute to Delfina's ongoing programme. WHO: visual artists and curators
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; duo appli
 cations not possible\; application must be in English. One work period ava
 ilable: 27 September to 17 December 2027. Selection by an advisory committ
 ee with a Delfina representative\; processing may exceed three months. DEA
 DLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00 Dutch time / 11:00 Caribbean
  time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Lon
 don\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherlands or the 
 Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subs
 idy of EUR 9\,188 for an artist or EUR 7\,232 for a curator/art observer t
 oward travel\, material and living costs (a 10 percent personal contributi
 on is automatically deducted by the Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living spac
 e and Delfina Foundation support are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. 
 Contribution for Caribbean-based artists can be increased for higher trave
 l costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 27 September to 17 D
 ecember 2027\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/g
 rants/residency/delfina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/del
 fina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherla
 nds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
 ingen/residency/inside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regelingen/residency/i
 nside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curators and critics based i
 n the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mon
 driaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:avistavulcao-azores-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:Deadline: AVISTAVULCÃO: Azores Artist Residency 2027 (Faial\, Port
 ugal)
DESCRIPTION:AVISTAVULCÃO opens a call for a one-month artist-in-residence 
 programme focused on research and creation\, taking place in March 2027 an
 d intended for an artist or artistic duo. Located on the island of Faial n
 ear the Capelinhos Volcano (Azores\, Portugal)\, the residency offers imme
 rsion in a territory shaped by geology\, insularity\, and the interplay be
 tween nature and human presence\, with the Azores treated as living materi
 al for creation. Artists are invited to develop projects engaging with lan
 dscape\, memory\, local history\, and the contemporary challenges facing p
 eripheral regions\; suggested starting points include geological time\, tr
 ansformation\, resilience\, isolation\, mobility\, and the relationships b
 etween communities and the environment. Context-sensitive proposals that p
 rioritise observation\, listening and a relationship with the place are va
 lued. Residents meet local stakeholders and share moments with the communi
 ty\, culminating in a public presentation of the process or results. SUPPO
 RT (in-person mobility): EUR 1\,350 allowance per resident\, travel allowa
 nce of EUR 400 to 800\, green mobility top-up of EUR 400\, visa top-up of 
 EUR 120 per resident\, outermost regions top-up of EUR 175 per resident\, 
 family top-up of EUR 200 per child\, and accessibility support. ELIGIBILIT
 Y: individual artists and duos (cross-disciplinary welcome) from countries
  eligible for the Creative Europe programme. DEADLINE: 1 August 2026.\n\nO
 rganisation: AVISTAVULCÃO / Barca 13\nLocation: Faial Island\, Azores\, P
 ortugal (near the Capelinhos Volcano). Open to artists from countries elig
 ible for the Creative Europe programme.\nAward: EUR 1\,350 allowance per r
 esident for the month\, plus travel allowance (EUR 400 to 800)\, green mob
 ility top-up (EUR 400)\, visa top-up (EUR 120/resident)\, outermost region
 s and overseas territories top-up (EUR 175/resident)\, family top-up (EUR 
 200 per child/resident)\, and accessibility support. No application fee.\n
 Duration: One month\, March 2027\n\nMore: https://www.barca13.pt/en/avista
 vulcao/agora/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.barca13.pt/en/avistavulcao/agora/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Faial Island\, Azores\, Portugal (near the Capelinhos Volcano). Op
 en to artists from countries eligible for the Creative Europe programme.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cmc-dmarc-sonic-arts-residency-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260805
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260806
SUMMARY:Deadline: CMC/DMARC Sonic Arts Residency 2026/2027
DESCRIPTION:The Digital Media and Arts Research Centre (DMARC) and CMC Irel
 and announce the second year of the Sonic Arts Residency Programme at the 
 University of Limerick Electronic Music Studio for 2026/27. The residency 
 offers Irish and international composers and sound artists an opportunity 
 to develop their creative practice and experiment using UL's facilities. F
 ACILITIES: the Electronic Music Studio (EMS) featuring both digital and an
 alogue workflows\, including a bespoke Buchla 200e\; a 32-channel immersiv
 e sound lab (SpADE)\; a makerspace supporting electronics and fabrication\
 ; and a range of well-equipped recording studios with a wide selection of 
 microphones and production hardware and software. DMARC is based in the Co
 mputer Science and Information Systems Department at UL and has a long his
 tory supporting digital arts\, electronic music\, and computer-aided compo
 sition (hosting the 2022 International Computer Music Conference and 2020 
 International Conference on Live Coding\, the Diffusion Prize with RTE Lyr
 ic FM\, and partnering with Light Moves Festival). PROGRAMME: each residen
 cy lasts 10 working days within one of two windows\, September-December 20
 26 or January-March 2027. Support includes a EUR 1\,000 honorarium from CM
 C\, a travel bursary up to EUR 350\, and an accommodation bursary up to EU
 R 1\,400 (ten nights)\, with DMARC helping identify accommodation. There i
 s an outreach/presentation element: a one-hour talk/performance for the DM
 ARC community of students and researchers\, and required documentation of 
 the process (photo\, video\, recordings\, and/or written reflections) that
  may be published by CMC on social media\; artists may also be invited to 
 contribute to CMC's amplify podcast series or online features at cmc.ie/fe
 atures. The programme runs 2025-27 with support for six artists (4 Irish\,
  2 international). ASSESSMENT: candidates apply via an online form submitt
 ing a CV\, work samples\, an outline of the residency project (including t
 echnical requirements)\, how they propose to engage with the facilities\, 
 and how the residency would benefit their practice. Criteria: artistic qua
 lity of the proposal including development of work using either the SpADE 
 system or Buchla 200e\; how the opportunity supports the candidate's curre
 nt career stage and artistic goals\; demonstrated technical capacity to en
 gage with the facilities\; and balanced representation of genres\, gender\
 , and geographical regions. TO APPLY: complete the online application form
  linked from the opportunity page. Closing date: 11am (IST)\, 5 August 202
 6\; late applications will not be accepted. Questions: jurgen.simpson@ul.i
 e or kfennell@cmc.ie. Applications are jointly assessed by DMARC and the C
 ontemporary Music Centre.\n\nOrganisation: Contemporary Music Centre (CMC)
  & Digital Media and Arts Research Centre (DMARC)\, University of Limerick
 \nLocation: University of Limerick\, Limerick\, Ireland (in person).\nAwar
 d: EUR 1\,000 honorarium (from CMC)\, plus a travel bursary up to EUR 350 
 and an accommodation bursary up to EUR 1\,400 (ten nights). No application
  fee.\nDuration: 10 working days\, scheduled within one of two windows: Se
 ptember-December 2026 or January-March 2027. Additional time may be reques
 ted where it does not incur extra cost.\n\nMore: http://cmc.ie/opportuniti
 es/open-call-cmcdmarc-sonic-arts-residency-20262027?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://cmc.ie/opportunities/open-call-cmcdmarc-sonic-arts-residency-202
 62027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:University of Limerick\, Limerick\, Ireland (in person).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:atheras-nicosia-ludic-lab-toyful-music-festival-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Atheras: Nicosia Ludic Lab for Composers\, Toyful Music F
 estival 2026
DESCRIPTION:Atheras Peoples and Cultures invites composers and performer-re
 searchers to apply for the Nicosia Ludic Lab\, a 31-day international resi
 dency dedicated to exploring 'play' as a compositional and performative me
 thodology in contemporary music. Building on the artistic vision of the To
 yful Music Festival\, the residency creates a focused environment where ex
 perimentation\, precision\, and imagination coexist\, redefining how music
  is conceived\, structured\, and performed. The residency runs in Nicosia\
 , Cyprus\, from 23 October to 22 November 2026\, and participants develop 
 new ensemble works that directly shape the artistic programme of the Toyfu
 l Music Festival 2026. ELIGIBILITY: applications are open to individual ar
 tists (proposals from duets or collectives will not be considered) based i
 n a Creative Europe country\, who must demonstrate a strong interest in ex
 perimental\, ensemble-based practices. SELECTED RESIDENTS RECEIVE: full fi
 nancial support (travel\, accommodation\, daily allowance)\; shared accomm
 odation in central Nicosia\; continuous access to a professional ensemble\
 ; mentorship sessions and individual meetings with ensemble members\; coac
 hing sessions with composer and conductor Andys Skordis\; artistic and pro
 fessional guidance from the Atheras team\; rehearsal space and full produc
 tion support for Phase 3\; and video and audio recording of the final live
  concert for documentation and international visibility. Deadline: 15 July
  2026.\n\nOrganisation: Atheras Peoples and Cultures\nLocation: Nicosia\, 
 Cyprus\; open to individual artists based in a Creative Europe country\nAw
 ard: Full financial support: travel\, shared accommodation in central Nico
 sia\, and daily allowance. Rehearsal space and full production support pro
 vided\; final live concert recorded (video and audio) for documentation an
 d international visibility.\nDuration: 31-day residency\, 23 October to 22
  November 2026\n\nMore: https://on-the-move.org/news/atheras-nicosia-ludic
 -lab-composers-new-works-toyful-music-festival-2026-cyprus?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://on-the-move.org/news/atheras-nicosia-ludic-lab-composers-new-wo
 rks-toyful-music-festival-2026-cyprus?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nicosia\, Cyprus\; open to individual artists based in a Creative 
 Europe country
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cmrfe-multispecies-residency-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260705
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260706
SUMMARY:Deadline: Artist Residency Autumn 2026 (Centre for Multispecies Rel
 ations and Future Ecologies\, Palermo)
DESCRIPTION:The Centre for Multispecies Relations and Future Ecologies invi
 tes applications from two artists for a 62-day residency (12 October - 12 
 December 2026) at its site in the Altarello di Baida district of Palermo\,
  Sicily. The residency is structured around a 1\,500 sqm garden at the thr
 eshold between the city's urban expansion and the historic rural landscape
  of the surrounding hills\; the site\, degraded through previous use (soil
  compaction and significant biodiversity loss)\, functions as both studio 
 and subject\, and artists participate in an ongoing process of ecological 
 transformation\, producing interventions that emerge from extended observa
 tion and fieldwork. Applications are welcome across all mediums and discip
 lines (installation\, sound\, performance\, video\, food art\, participato
 ry practice\, and beyond)\; research-based and interdisciplinary practices
  are especially encouraged. The Centre works at the intersection of art\, 
 science\, and (agro)ecological practices\, with a focus on multispecies co
 existence and climate change in the Mediterranean\, and has been based in 
 Palermo since 2021. PROGRAMME: five phases (orientation with small trips a
 nd gatherings\; observation with independent fieldwork and consultations w
 ith artists\, curators\, scientists\, and anthropologists\; proposal and e
 cological feasibility developed with mentors\; creation\; and public resti
 tution with an open event\, a workshop\, and a public discussion). Each ar
 tist develops an independent site-specific intervention\; the two resident
 s share the site\, living space\, and process\, with exchange encouraged b
 ut not prescribed. Artist duos and artists who want to collaborate are enc
 ouraged to apply (you can apply as an individual for one position\, as a d
 uo for both\, or as two artists collaborating for two positions). Mentorsh
 ip by co-founders/artistic directors Fabio Aranzulla and Luca Cinquemani (
 weekly site visits\, studio discussions\, work-in-progress presentations)\
 ; logistics managed by Francesca Farris. WHO: artists whose work engages w
 ith ecology\, multispecies relations\, or the more-than-human\, who can mo
 ve between observation and making and are interested in dialogue with scie
 ntists\, land workers\, and local communities. Priority is given to artist
 s from working-class and less-privileged backgrounds\, those who self-iden
 tify as part of marginalised communities\, and candidates reflecting diver
 sity in gender\, age\, geographical background\, and ability\; green trave
 l is prioritised as a condition of participation where feasible. Applicant
 s should be open to living and working in a neighbourhood on the margins o
 f Palermo's periphery. Funded by Culture Moves Europe (Creative Europe pro
 gramme of the European Union). APPLICATION: first phase via the online for
 m (opened 10 June)\; shortlisted artists contacted before the end of July\
 ; second phase is video calls with shortlisted candidates\; applications a
 ccepted in English and Italian. Contact: contact.cmrfe@gmail.com. Deadline
  5 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Centre for Multispecies Relations and Futur
 e Ecologies\nLocation: Altarello di Baida district\, Palermo\, Sicily\, It
 aly. On-site 62-day residency\, 12 October - 12 December 2026. Open to all
  nationalities\, but applicants must be officially residing in a Creative 
 Europe country (excluding Italy).\nAward: Total allowance of EUR 1\,860 (b
 efore tax) per artist\, plus a travel budget of EUR 400 per artist (for di
 stances under 4\,000 km) with a EUR 400 green-mobility top-up\, plus a pro
 duction budget. Also provided: on-site accommodation in a fully furnished 
 independent house (private bedroom\; shared kitchen\, living room\, two ba
 throoms\; outdoor studio space 100m from the working site)\, access to rec
 ycled/salvaged materials through the Centre's partnerships\, a bicycle per
  resident\, and a final public event.\nDuration: 62-day residency\, 12 Oct
 ober - 12 December 2026\, structured in five phases (orientation\, observa
 tion/fieldwork\, proposal and ecological feasibility\, creation\, and publ
 ic restitution).\n\nMore: https://tally.so/r/81r5Mz?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tally.so/r/81r5Mz?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Altarello di Baida district\, Palermo\, Sicily\, Italy. On-site 62
 -day residency\, 12 October - 12 December 2026. Open to all nationalities\
 , but applicants must be officially residing in a Creative Europe country 
 (excluding Italy).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vfa-sonic-connections-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sonic Connections Open Call 2027 (Villa Filanda Antonini)
DESCRIPTION:Villa Filanda Antonini (VFA) launches its Spring Open Call to s
 elect up to 4 artists and professionals for a one-month residency in March
  2027 on the theme 'Sonic Connections'\, focused on experimental music\, s
 ound art\, and performances. Hosted at Villa Filanda Antonini\, a former s
 ilk mill in Villorba\, Italy\, the project brings together four internatio
 nal artists and professionals to examine the relationship between architec
 ture\, landscape\, and collective sonic experience. ADDRESSED TO: artists\
 , performers\, curators\, designers\, and professionals not currently resi
 ding in Italy. GRANT & BENEFITS: a fully funded residency covering mentori
 ng\, accommodation\, travel costs\, production costs\, and a daily salary\
 , plus a EUR 1\,000 residency stipend. WHEN: 1-31 March 2027. HOW TO APPLY
 : complete the application form and attach a CV\, portfolio\, project prop
 osal\, and letter of reference. The VFA residency program has been selecte
 d under conditions by Culture Moves Europe\, a project funded by the Europ
 ean Union and implemented by the Goethe-Institut. Deadline: 19 July 2026\,
  23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Villa Filanda Antonini (VFA)\nLocation: Vill
 orba\, Italy (a former silk mill). Addressed to artists and professionals 
 NOT currently residing in Italy.\nAward: Fully funded residency covering m
 entoring\, accommodation\, travel costs\, production costs\, and a daily s
 alary\, plus a EUR 1\,000 residency stipend.\nDuration: One-month residenc
 y\, 1-31 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.vfa.art/events/sonic-connections
 -open-call-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.vfa.art/events/sonic-connections-open-call-2027/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Villorba\, Italy (a former silk mill). Addressed to artists and pr
 ofessionals NOT currently residing in Italy.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ay-roop-le-milieu-reuse-circus-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260703
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260704
SUMMARY:Deadline: AY-ROOP / Le Milieu: Reuse - (Re)making for Circus Reside
 ncy 2026 (Rennes Métropole\, France)
DESCRIPTION:AY-ROOP is launching an open call to select three circus artist
 s and/or circus set designers/builders for a 21-day Culture Moves Europe r
 esearch residency at Le Milieu (Saint-Jacques-de-la-Lande\, Rennes Métrop
 ole) from 28 November to 18 December 2026. The residency is a research lab
 oratory on reuse in contemporary circus: how everyday\, locally available 
 materials (paper/cardboard\, plastics\, lightweight metal\, textiles\, rec
 laimed wood\, bicycle parts\, etc.) can be used to create scenographic ele
 ments\, sets\, props and small apparatuses for juggling\, acrobatics and b
 alancing. The core principle is that objects are recreated locally from re
 sources available in each territory rather than transported. AY-ROOP provi
 des an equipped construction workshop\, a rehearsal stage and circus tent\
 , a guide to local reuse-sector contacts\, and a full residency environmen
 t (accommodation\, shared kitchen\, working facilities)\; two mentors (a r
 euse specialist and a performing-arts professional) support the artists. P
 ROFILES: circus artists interested in construction/scenography/DIY making\
 , and builders/set designers working in circus\; individual or group appli
 cations (max 3 people per group)\; emerging or established\, any backgroun
 d. Accessible to artists with disabilities and accessibility needs. Workin
 g language English. No aerial apparatus or rigging: all work is ground-bas
 ed. ELIGIBILITY: aged 18+ (no upper limit)\; legally resident in a Creativ
 e Europe country other than France and DROM-COM\; available for the full r
 esidency. APPLY with a single PDF (1-page bio/CV\, 5-page portfolio or vid
 eo links\, 1-page statement of intent\, proof of residence). DEADLINE: 3 J
 uly 2026. Results announced 13 July 2026. Check the linked call PDF for fu
 ll details.\n\nOrganisation: AY-ROOP\nLocation: Le Milieu\, Saint-Jacques-
 de-la-Lande\, Rennes Métropole\, France. Applicants must legally reside i
 n a Creative Europe country other than France and the French overseas terr
 itories (DROM-COM).\nAward: Funded through Culture Moves Europe: EUR 900 m
 obility allowance per person plus flat-rate travel coverage\; supplements 
 for green mobility\, visa fees\, dependent children under 18\, OCT/OR resi
 dents\, and disability/accessibility needs (including possible full covera
 ge of a sign-language interpreter). On-site single-room accommodation\, lu
 nches at Le Milieu canteen (Tuesday to Friday)\, shared kitchen\, and tech
 nical support provided. No application fee.\nDuration: 21-day residency\, 
 28 November to 18 December 2026.\n\nMore: https://circusdance.fi/ilmoituks
 et/ay-roop-le-milieu-rennes-metropole-france-open-call-for-circus-artists-
 and-set-designers-for-a-residency-focused-on-the-reuse-of-materials-nov-de
 c-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://circusdance.fi/ilmoitukset/ay-roop-le-milieu-rennes-metropole-f
 rance-open-call-for-circus-artists-and-set-designers-for-a-residency-focus
 ed-on-the-reuse-of-materials-nov-dec-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Le Milieu\, Saint-Jacques-de-la-Lande\, Rennes Métropole\, France
 . Applicants must legally reside in a Creative Europe country other than F
 rance and the French overseas territories (DROM-COM).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mota-production-residency-ljubljana-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: MoTA Museum of Transitory Art: Production Residency 2027 
 (Ljubljana)
DESCRIPTION:MoTA (Museum of Transitory Art) in Ljubljana runs an annual ope
 n call for production residencies for media\, sound and visual artists\, c
 urators and researchers. Production residencies offer full support includi
 ng accommodation\, technical support\, production costs and an artist fee\
 ; the exact artist-fee amount is not published on the official or aggregat
 or pages\, so applicants should confirm the figure directly by email. Resi
 dencies run up to one month. Open internationally: artists of all national
 ities and at all professional levels are encouraged to apply\, as individu
 als or collectives. No application fee. The annual deadline is 15 Septembe
 r (for residencies the following year). Apply by email to mota.artists@gma
 il.com with the subject line Application for production residency. Note: t
 he official motamuseum.com SSL certificate is currently expired\, which ma
 y briefly affect link reliability.\n\nOrganisation: MoTA - Museum of Trans
 itory Art\nLocation: Ljubljana\, Slovenia. Open internationally to artists
  of all nationalities and professional levels.\nAward: Full support includ
 ing accommodation\, technical support\, production costs and an artist fee
 . The exact EUR artist-fee amount is not published\; confirm by email. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Production residency of up to one month.\n\nMo
 re: http://motamuseum.com/RESIDENCY/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://motamuseum.com/RESIDENCY/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ljubljana\, Slovenia. Open internationally to artists of all natio
 nalities and professional levels.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:q-o2-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Q-O2: Residency Programme 2027 (Experimental Music & Soun
 d Art)
DESCRIPTION:The residencies at Q-O2 offer time and space for artistic resea
 rch\, reflection and creation in the field of experimental music and sound
  art. In 2027\, Q-O2 will host 20 residencies\, 10 for international artis
 ts and 10 for local artists living in Belgium\, working with\, on or aroun
 d sound. The programme is open to artists\, art workers and theorists who 
 wish to pursue a research-oriented project\; note that Q-O2 does not organ
 ise production-directed residencies and is not a rehearsal space. Duos are
  possible\, and exceptionally small groups too. SUPPORT: a work studio and
  materials\, a creative and communicative environment\, and the possibilit
 y to present work to a public and/or propose a workshop\; for internationa
 l residents\, accommodation in a shared apartment and a contribution to tr
 avel expenses of up to EUR 200\; and a small subsistence budget reserved f
 or artists who do not come with other funding. There is no artist fee. A f
 inal public presentation can be arranged if the artist wishes but is not e
 xpected\; what Q-O2 requires are some traces of the residency in word\, im
 age and/or audio form. APPLY by 15 September 2026: email a concise project
  proposal of no more than one page plus a permanent link to your website o
 r other secondary information (no temporary links) to info@q-o2.be with th
 e subject 'Residency27 - your name'. State where you would travel from\, h
 ow long you would like to stay (4 to 6 weeks)\, and your interest in Q-O2 
 as a working environment\, and make sure you receive an email confirmation
  of receipt.\n\nOrganisation: Q-O2 (workspace for experimental music and s
 ound art)\nLocation: Brussels\, Belgium\; 10 residencies for international
  artists and 10 for artists living in Belgium.\nAward: NO artist fee. Inte
 rnational residents: shared accommodation in the Q-O2 apartment plus a tra
 vel contribution up to EUR 200. A small subsistence budget is reserved for
  artists who do not come with other funding. Work studio\, materials and t
 echnical equipment provided. No application fee.\nDuration: Usually 3 to 6
  weeks (international applicants: 4 to 6 weeks\; stays over 4 weeks not gu
 aranteed)\n\nMore: https://www.q-o2.be/en/in-residency/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.q-o2.be/en/in-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Brussels\, Belgium\; 10 residencies for international artists and 
 10 for artists living in Belgium.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:icst-artists-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: ICST: Artists in Residence 2027 Open Call (ZHdK\, Zurich)
DESCRIPTION:The Institute for Computer Music and Sound Technology (ICST) at
  the Zurich University of the Arts (ZHdK) invites applications for its 202
 7 Artists in Residence program\, fostering artistic exchange in key areas 
 of current research. Residencies are available in five themes: Spatial Aud
 io\; Klavierautomat (algorithmic composition)\; Moving Loudspeakers\; Danc
 e and Generative AI\; and Object Performance. The program offers access to
  ICST's facilities and technical infrastructure\, professional support fro
 m researchers\, and per diems for meals and accommodation. Artists and mus
 icians working with sound and sound media\, whose practice reflects a stro
 ng interest in one of the listed research areas\, are encouraged to apply.
  One selected project from the Spatial Audio Residency will be featured at
  the SONIC MATTER Festival 2028 as part of an ongoing partnership. PRACTIC
 AL: residencies include use of facilities and technical infrastructure as 
 specified in the thematic descriptions\, plus technical support by ICST re
 search staff. Participants receive a contribution toward travel to Zurich 
 (up to CHF 300 for persons living in Europe\, up to CHF 500 for persons li
 ving outside Europe) and a per diem to cover meals and accommodation in Zu
 rich\; participants organise their own travel and accommodation\, with ICS
 T assistance if required. Residency dates are defined individually. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted via the online form\, uploading a concept sketch\, compos
 ition idea or project draft (PDF\, 2 pages\, 10 MB max)\; a portfolio of t
 hree selected works relevant to the residency topic including links to ext
 ernal audio and video (PDF\, 2 pages\, 10 MB max)\; and a tabular CV cover
 ing education and career (PDF\, 1 page\, 10 MB max). The residencies are a
 warded by a jury of ICST researchers and project leaders. TIMELINE: deadli
 ne 1 September 2026 at 24:00 CET\; candidates notified mid-October 2026. S
 elected candidates receive forms required for an invitation to Switzerland
  and must confirm participation and return completed forms within 10 days 
 or the invitation may be withdrawn.\n\nOrganisation: Institute for Compute
 r Music and Sound Technology (ICST)\, Zurich University of the Arts (ZHdK)
 \nLocation: Zurich\, Switzerland (in-person residency at ICST)\nAward: Use
  of ICST facilities and technical infrastructure plus technical support by
  research staff\; per diems for meals and accommodation during the residen
 cy\; travel contribution toward travel to Zurich (up to CHF 300 for person
 s living in Europe\, up to CHF 500 for those outside Europe). Participants
  organise their own travel and accommodation (ICST assists if required). N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Residency dates defined individually with se
 lected candidates\n\nMore: https://www.zhdk.ch/en/research/icst/icst-air/c
 onditions-selection-process-20736?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://www.zhdk.ch/en/research/icst/icst-air/conditions-selection-proc
 ess-20736?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zurich\, Switzerland (in-person residency at ICST)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAP / EMARE: European Media Art Platform Residencies 202
 7
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Platform (EMAP/EMARE) is a network of le
 ading European media-art organisations offering fully funded two-month pro
 duction residencies for artists working with digital media\, including med
 ia art\, bio art and robotic art. Each residency provides a EUR 4\,000 gra
 nt to the applying artist (including subsistence)\, a EUR 4\,000 project b
 udget\, host-provided accommodation\, travel covered according to EU ceili
 ngs\, and access to technical facilities and media labs\; a collaborating 
 artist receives an additional EUR 2\,000 (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo). Res
 idencies take place at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, France
 \, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, the Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, 
 Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland. ELIGIBILITY
 : applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state\, or 
 residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries (Netherlands-b
 ased artists qualify). Undergraduate and Master's students are not eligibl
 e\; PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background
  may apply. IMPORTANT: applicants must apply as a duo or collective\, or p
 ropose a collaborative project\, rather than as a purely solo applicant. T
 he 2027 open call runs from 3 September 2026 to 6 November 2026 at 14:00 C
 ET. Apply online at call.emare.eu. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Eu
 ropean Media Art Platform (EMAP / EMARE)\nLocation: Two-month production r
 esidency at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, France\, Slovakia
 \, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\,
  Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland\nAward: EUR 4\,000 grant fo
 r the applying artist (including subsistence)\; EUR 2\,000 for a collabora
 ting artist (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo)\; EUR 4\,000 project budget\; acc
 ommodation provided by the host\; travel covered per EU ceilings\; access 
 to technical facilities and media labs. No application fee.\nDuration: Two
  months\n\nMore: https://emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
LOCATION:Two-month production residency at one of 15 host institutions acro
 ss Austria\, France\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Sloven
 ia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Pola
 nd
END:VEVENT
