UID:stichting-stokroos-residency-fundaziun-nairs-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Residency at Fundaziun Nairs 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos funds a three-month reflective residency at 
 Fundaziun Nairs in Scuol\, Switzerland\, for one selected visual artist\, 
 designer or craft practitioner (overlap possible). Both emerging and estab
 lished makers may apply. Stokroos covers full accommodation and meals dire
 ctly with Fundaziun Nairs and provides a discretionary EUR 7\,000 budget f
 or living\, travel and production. The application should include a propos
 al that engages specifically with the residency\, its Alpine surroundings 
 and/or its historical and cultural context. Eligibility: you completed you
 r first subject-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2022 or earli
 er\, or have an equivalent established practice\, or started without forma
 l training (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at leas
 t 21 years old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (inc
 luding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not curren
 tly enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. Applications are indiv
 idual only\; duos and collectives cannot apply. Makers already selected by
  Fundaziun Nairs may still apply if they meet the criteria. You may submit
  only one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not h
 ave received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. Apply v
 ia the online form (Dutch or English) with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages\
 , optional video up to 10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages\, and work/plan
  descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each. Selection includes an introduc
 tory interview with up to three candidates\; Stokroos aims to respond with
 in 8 weeks. No appeal is possible. Application window: 1 to 11 September 2
 026. More information at nairs.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLo
 cation: Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.\nAward: Fully supported stay (accommodation and 
 meals paid directly to Fundaziun Nairs) plus an unrestricted living\, trav
 el and production budget of EUR 7\,000. 80% paid before the residency\, th
 e remainder on receipt of a brief final report. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Intensive three-month working period (July through September).\n\nMor
 e: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vac-belgrade-visual-anthropology-residency@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Visual Anthropology Center (VAC): Residency Programme (Be
 lgrade)
DESCRIPTION:Visual Anthropology Center (VAC) in Belgrade invites filmmakers
 \, visual anthropologists\, artists\, and researchers to apply for its res
 idency programme. The residency specialises in visual anthropology but is 
 also open to individual and collaborative projects in experimental ethnogr
 aphy\, creative documentary film\, and other artistic mediums. Residents m
 ay apply with a project aimed at a public showing\, or use the time and sp
 ace to reflect\, research\, or write without a specific outcome. WHAT IS P
 ROVIDED: accommodation and studio space in central Belgrade\; additional w
 orkspace and community connection through Community Center KROV (an indepe
 ndent creative hub hosting lectures\, events\, and exhibitions)\; project 
 guidance and mentorship from film professionals\, ethnomusicologists\, pro
 ducers\, artists\, curators\, and anthropologists\; connections to local c
 ultural and academic institutions\, archives\, galleries\, and exhibition 
 spaces\; access to camera equipment\, translators for fieldwork or editing
 \, fixers\, and project-specific services or materials\; opportunity to ex
 hibit a final project as an exhibition\, installation\, screening\, worksh
 op\, or lecture. Eligible projects may be promoted through VAC's platforms
  and partner networks\, including the Vizantrop Film Festival\, for region
 al and international visibility. ELIGIBILITY: filmmakers\, visual anthropo
 logists\, artists\, and researchers\; individual and collaborative project
 s welcome. Applications accepted on a rolling basis.\n\nOrganisation: Visu
 al Anthropology Center (VAC)\nLocation: Belgrade\, Serbia (accommodation a
 nd studio in central Belgrade\; additional workspace at Community Center K
 ROV)\nAward: EUR 1\,000–1\,500 per month (stipend\, varies by project re
 quirements)\, plus accommodation and studio space provided. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Approximately 1–2 months\; flexible packages depending 
 on project needs\n\nMore: https://vac.rs/program/residency?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://vac.rs/program/residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Belgrade\, Serbia (accommodation and studio in central Belgrade\; 
 additional workspace at Community Center KROV)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stiftung-kuenstlerdorf-schoeppingen-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stiftung Künstler*dorf Schöppingen: Residency Fellowshi
 p 2027 Open Call
DESCRIPTION:Stiftung Künstler*dorf Schöppingen offers residency fellowshi
 ps for professional visual artists\, authors and composers\; since 2023 ap
 plications from collectives are also accepted. The call is open to people 
 of all nationalities and ages\, and accommodation for partners\, family me
 mbers or assistance can be arranged upon agreement and availability (for p
 hysical\, cognitive or sensory disabilities\, contact the foundation to ex
 plain any barriers). Fellows reside and work at the Künstler*dorf for a p
 eriod of their choosing between two and six months\, using the premises an
 d infrastructure on-site. The stipend is EUR 1\,500 per month\, minus roug
 hly EUR 100-200 for rent and operating expenses\; for collectives it is EU
 R 1\,000 per person up to a maximum of EUR 3\,000 per month\, minus rent a
 nd operating costs. Travel\, insurance or material costs are covered only 
 in exceptional cases on request. The fellowship is not designed as a produ
 ction residency and there is no obligation to present results\, though exh
 ibition and presentation facilities are available and the voluntary co-org
 anization of events (lectures\, readings\, workshops or similar) is welcom
 ed. A willingness to participate in events and to engage in exchange with 
 other fellows is a prerequisite. Selection is made by expert juries on the
  quality of previous work\, the quality and plausibility of the project fo
 r Schöppingen\, and program contributions (interaction / community buildi
 ng). Applications for 2027 can be submitted from 27 June to 31 August 2026
  (midnight CET) via the online application portal.\n\nOrganisation: Stiftu
 ng Künstler*dorf Schöppingen\nLocation: Schöppingen\, Germany (residenc
 y requires living and working on-site)\nAward: Stipend of EUR 1\,500 per m
 onth\, minus roughly EUR 100-200 for rent and operating expenses. For coll
 ectives\, EUR 1\,000 per person up to a maximum of EUR 3\,000 per month\, 
 minus rent and operating costs. Travel\, insurance and material costs are 
 covered only in exceptional cases\, on request.\nDuration: Residency of tw
 o to six months during 2027\; period chosen by agreement and availability\
 n\nMore: https://stiftung-kuenstlerdorf.de/en/application_process?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stiftung-kuenstlerdorf.de/en/application_process?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Schöppingen\, Germany (residency requires living and working on-s
 ite)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Residency grant supports professional visu
 al artists\, curators\, and art observers who want to deepen their practic
 e through a residency in the Netherlands or abroad. It contributes to the 
 costs of a self-arranged residency that offers meaningful development for 
 the applicant's work. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists\, curators\, and art o
 bservers who have been professionally active for at least one year and are
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. AMOUNT: th
 e grant amount varies depending on the residency's location and duration\;
  applicants must contribute at least 10% of the costs themselves\, through
  personal investment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\,
  or crowdfunding. APPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online 
 application portal\, which requires a pre-created account (allow several w
 orking days). DEADLINE: 27 August 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (11:00 Caribbean
  time).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Nethe
 rlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherlands or abroad.\
 nAward: Grant amount varies depending on the location and duration of the 
 residency. Applicants must contribute at least 10% themselves (personal in
 vestment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\, or crowdfun
 ding).\nDuration: Varies by residency.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds
 .nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Ca
 ribbean part of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherland
 s or abroad.
END:VEVENT
