UID:zamek-artist-residency-poznan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260728
SUMMARY:Deadline: ZAMEK Artist Residency 2027 (ZAMEK Culture Centre\, Pozna
 n)
DESCRIPTION:Open call for ZAMEK Culture Centre's 2027 Artist-in-Residence p
 rogramme in Poznan. Supports artists working across visual arts\, performa
 nce\, choreography\, dance\, music\, sound art\, architecture and filmmaki
 ng (literature is excluded). Two formats: a Conceptual Residency (creative
  stay\, no requirement to complete or present a final work\, with public m
 eetings at least every two weeks) and an Operational Residency (concluding
  with an artistic event such as an exhibition\, concert or screening\, plu
 s regular public meetings). Selected artists receive accommodation in the 
 former imperial residence\, a studio\, a fee of PLN 6\,000 gross per month
 \, a production budget of PLN 5\,000 to 15\,000 gross\, curatorial support
  and publicity. Residencies run 4 to 8 weeks in 2027. ZAMEK is particularl
 y interested in projects that engage changing realities\, the current mome
 nt and the future (climate and migration crises\, the war in Ukraine\, soc
 ial and political issues) or the context\, history and architecture of the
  Castle\; project scale must fit the programme budget\, and projects shoul
 d not rely on external co-financing. Download the Terms & Conditions on th
 e ZAMEK site to apply. Deadline: 27 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: ZAMEK Cult
 ure Centre (Centrum Kultury ZAMEK)\nLocation: Poznan\, Poland\nAward: Acco
 mmodation in an apartment in the former imperial residence\, studio access
 \, a fee of PLN 6\,000 gross per month (contract for specific work)\, a pr
 oduction budget of PLN 5\,000 to 15\,000 gross depending on length of stay
  and project\, plus curatorial support and publicity. No application fee l
 isted.\nDuration: 4 to 8 weeks during 2027 (Conceptual or Operational Resi
 dency format)\n\nMore: https://ckzamek.pl/artykuly/14724-open-call-rezyden
 cje-artystyczne-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://ckzamek.pl/artykuly/14724-open-call-rezydencje-artystyczne-2027
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Poznan\, Poland
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:apostaxis-residency-exhibition-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260727
SUMMARY:Deadline: APOSTAXIS Artist Residency & Exhibition 2026 (Ukraine / C
 yprus)
DESCRIPTION:APOSTAXIS is an international residency and exhibition programm
 e exploring displacement\, memory\, identity and cultural resilience. It s
 elects four visual artists (three from Ukraine and one from Cyprus) for tw
 o simultaneous 20-day residencies in Ternopil\, Ukraine and Larnaca\, Cypr
 us (6 to 28 October 2026)\, followed by post-production\, a digital exhibi
 tion\, and a curated physical exhibition in Larnaca in January 2027. ELIGI
 BILITY: visual artists from Ukraine and Cyprus with lived experience or fa
 mily heritage connected to displacement\, working in community-engaged or 
 research-based practices (installation\, mixed media\, participatory\, soc
 ial practice\, documentary\, performance\, archive-based work). Artists un
 able to travel due to war-related restrictions or personal circumstances r
 emain eligible via hybrid participation. Fully funded: EUR 1\,800 artist f
 ee (equivalent UAH for Ukrainian artists)\, EUR 300 production budget\, tr
 avel\, accommodation\, meals and curatorial support\; no application fee. 
 Deadline: 26 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: ZMINA (Ukraine) with Cypriot part
 ner organisation\nLocation: Ternopil\, Ukraine and Larnaca\, Cyprus (hybri
 d participation possible)\nAward: Fully funded: artist fee of EUR 1\,800 (
 including tax\; paid in equivalent UAH for Ukrainian artists)\, EUR 300 pr
 oduction budget\, plus travel\, accommodation\, meals and curatorial suppo
 rt. No application fee.\nDuration: 20-day residency\, 6 to 28 October 2026
 \, with a group exhibition in Larnaca in January 2027\n\nMore: https://art
 infoland.com/opportunities/apostaxis-artist-residency-2026-ukraine-cyprus?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artinfoland.com/opportunities/apostaxis-artist-residency-2026-u
 kraine-cyprus?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ternopil\, Ukraine and Larnaca\, Cyprus (hybrid participation poss
 ible)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T213546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
